<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main id="main-content">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Seafarers</li></ol></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Amicus solutions for seafarers</p>
      <h1>For the journey between vessel and home.</h1>
      <p class="lead">A crew change can take you from a vessel and launch boat to a port terminal, hotel and several airports. Amicus brings together connectivity, travel preparation and coordination tools for that journey.</p>
      <div class="inline-links"><a class="button button-primary" href="<%= site.shopUrl %>" data-event="buy_esim_click">Find an eSIM plan</a><a class="text-link" href="#crew-preparation">Prepare for your crew change</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="seafarer-journey-heading" id="crew-preparation">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Joining, travelling, signing off</p><h2 id="seafarer-journey-heading">Keep the next handover clear.</h2><p>Connectivity matters when you need to find the pickup point, reach your agent or tell family you have arrived. Prepare for the gaps between reliable connections.</p><%- include('partials/media', { media: media.crewConnectivity }) %></div>
      <ol class="numbered-list">
        <li><h3>Before leaving home or the vessel</h3><p>Save joining instructions, tickets, the meeting point and your coordinator's contact details offline. Read the data plan's device, destination and activation guidance while you have an internet connection.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Between airport, hotel and port</h3><p>Check coverage for the transit country as well as the joining country. Keep the person arranging your transfer informed when travel times change; an app update does not confirm a new pickup.</p></li>
        <li><h3>After sign-off or during shore leave</h3><p>Check whether your plan is still valid and covers the next country. Arrange a way to contact the ship or coordinator before you leave, including a fallback if mobile data is unavailable.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-soft" aria-labelledby="seafarer-solutions-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your Amicus services</p><h2 id="seafarer-solutions-heading">Choose what you need for the next leg.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid-three">
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">Connectivity</p><h3>Buy and manage mobile data.</h3><p>The dedicated Amicus eSIM store handles current plans, prices, coverage, phone checks, setup and orders.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.shopUrl %>" data-event="buy_esim_click">Go to the Amicus eSIM store</a></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">Coordination</p><h3>Understand Amicus Crew Change.</h3><p>See how participating crew and coordinators share trip information and journey updates before opening the application.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.crewLandingUrl %>">Explore the crew-change tool</a></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">Preparation</p><h3>Plan for a journey with several stops.</h3><p>Work through an itinerary country by country, including the connection where you may need to reach an agent or change a flight.</p><a class="text-link" href="/resources/crew-change-connectivity">Read the crew-change guide</a></article>
      </div>
      <div class="callout support-links"><div><h3>Already have an eSIM order?</h3><p>Your store account, installation instructions and order support are together in Amicus eSIM.</p></div><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.accountUrl %>" data-event="account_visit">Your eSIM account</a><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.installationUrl %>">Installation help</a><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.supportUrl %>" data-event="support_visit">Order &amp; connection support</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">Ship and shore are different</p><h2>Know where mobile data can help.</h2></div><div class="faq-list">
    <details><summary>Will a travel eSIM work while the vessel is at sea?</summary><div><p>Travel eSIMs use terrestrial mobile networks. They do not provide mid-ocean satellite service. Signal at a berth, anchorage or coast depends on local network reach and the plan; do not assume it is available because the ship is near land.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary>Where should I check prices, coverage and my phone?</summary><div><p>Use the current plan details and device guidance in the Amicus eSIM store. Your exact phone model, regional variant and carrier-unlock status matter.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.helpUrl %>">Read the store's compatibility guidance</a></div></details>
    <details><summary>Does the crew-change tool arrange my local transfer?</summary><div><p>The tool helps participating people coordinate the journey. Your agent or responsible coordinator must confirm the transport, meeting point and local arrangements. Registration alone does not book a transfer.</p></div></details>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="section section-dark"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Maritime experience behind Amicus</p><h2>Built with life around a port call in mind.</h2><p>Founder Jivko Atanassov's background spans ship agency, marine superintendent work and petroleum inspection.</p></div><div><a class="button button-light" href="/about">Meet Amicus Shipping</a></div></div></section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>